      {
        "id": 120280,
        "name": "Nielzabub",
        "username": "Nielzabub",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/{size}/1986_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-19T11:39:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just had a crazy game against Advanced Voss. It was Haka, G.I. Bunker, Visionary, Ra, and Tempest versus Voss. For a second, it looked like the heroes would fail. A Forced Deployment had put over 10 minions into play, and on that turn Voss played another Forced Deployment. Fortunatley, Tempest had an Into the Stratosphere in his hand. Even with Panzer Buster, I wasn't quite able to kill Voss in that first round with 39 HP, and so Haka Ground Pounded instead. Bunker killed the minions in play with an External Combustion so that Voss wouldn't win at the start of his turn, and also did Panzer Buster. My plan was to ignore the army and go straight for Voss, but I ended up doing so much more. Visionary had taken heavy damage, and had been in a cocoon for most of the game. Ra and Tempest did damage to Voss.</p><p>At the start of the next villain round, Forced Deployment brought out all the minions Bunker had killed. At the end of the villain turn, Voss had 13 minions and Vyktor in play. Haka used a Haka of Battle and a Taiaha to smack Voss and whittle down the Guard. Bunker finished off the guard with Gattling Gun, went into Turret Mode and hit Voss with the Omni-Cannon. Visionary had demoralize and hit almost everything for 1. That's when I realized I could do it. I could kill Voss, and all the minions. By the time it was Ra's turn, Voss was down to four HP,and so Ra weakened the Psi-worms that Visionary couldn't damage. On Tempest's turn, Tempest murdered everyone with Electrical storm, a Chain Lightning, and Grievous Hailstorm. Voss was utterly defeated and peace was restored to the Multiverse.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:42.577Z",
